   <narrative xml:lang="DE">Errichtung &#xdc;bertragungsleitung Armenien - Georgien und Hochspannungsgleichstrom&#xfc;bertragungsbr&#xfc;cke (HGKK)</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The FZ project Caucasus Energy Network (Caucasus Transmission Network Project) aims to create a reliable, flexible, and mutually beneficial cross-border energy exchange within the South Caucasus. The asynchronous Armenian and Georgian grids will be connected via a High Voltage Direct Current (HVDC) short coupling in Ayrum near the Georgian border. This project contributes to improving supply security and quality within the region, as well as to the more efficient use of generation capacities, particularly in Armenia, in line with the Caucasus Initiative of the Federal Government and the EU Neighborhood Policy, and supports further economic and social development.The investment consists of the HVDC short coupling, a substation in Ddmashen in central Armenia, the construction or rehabilitation of relevant transmission lines from Ddmashen to the Georgian border, additional related investments in the Armenian transmission network, and consulting services.</narrative>
  </description>
